{
  "_comment": "Cross-language conformance cases for the Profile filter. Both the Python pure matcher (profiles.matches_filter) and the TypeScript pure matcher (card-filter.profileMatches) must agree on every case, so a saved Profile selects the same tasks in a notification (server-side), the admin task list, and the dashboard card. Tasks here carry their EFFECTIVE label/area ids directly (own + any inherited from device/area), since each side resolves inheritance before/inside matching; these cases pin the shared matcher logic with empty registries. A filter is a status plus a list of GROUPS. One group ANDs its include lists (labels per labels_match: any = one listed label, all = every listed label; an empty list means any) and then subtracts its exclude_* lists and its exclude_shopping switch, which win inside that group only. The groups are ORed: the task matches when any ACTIVE group takes it, where a group is active when any of its lists is non-empty or exclude_shopping is on. A filter with no active group has no include gate and selects its whole status tier. now is a fixed instant so date math is deterministic.",
